Fixed and passing. 

**Cause:** `integratedGPUAllowedByDefault()` in `discover/runner.go` only admitted CUDA integrated GPUs by default. The ROCm Radeon 8060S (gfx1151) was not on the allowlist, so `filterIntegratedGPUs` dropped it in auto mode.

**Fix** (`discover/runner.go:412`): also allow integrated GPUs whose `GFXTarget` is a `gfx115x` target (the 8060S / Strix Halo class, gfx1151), while still dropping the 780M (gfx1103) in auto mode. Explicit `OLLAMA_IGPU_ENABLE` true/false behavior is unchanged.

```go
func integratedGPUAllowedByDefault(device ml.DeviceInfo) bool {
	// Integrated GPUs are allowed by default when the compute target is known
	// to work well, e.g. the AMD Radeon 8060S (gfx1151) or NVIDIA integrated.
	if strings.HasPrefix(device.GFXTarget, "gfx115") {
		return true
	}
	return device.Library == "CUDA"
}
```

`go test ./discover/...` → `ok`.
